    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000121630,
      "SummaryText": "This document comprises the Risk Management Plan (RMP) for the Specialty Sales Facility located in Dumas, Texas (hereinafter referred to as the facility or the subject site). The site is owned and operated by Specialty Sales LLC. The purpose of this document is to comply with the risk management planning and update requirements as set forth in Title 40 CFR Chapter 1 Part 68 (also known as the Chemical Accidental Prevention Provisions). The scope of the RMP includes all operations conducted at the subject site that involve the storage and handling of regulated substance(s).\nThe regulated substances (RS) stored and handled at the facility in excess of threshold quantities and subject to RMP are Formalin. This regulated substance is present within a mixture in a concentration less than 100%, delivered and stored at the subject site for resale to customers. Storage of this RS item is limited to an onsite exterior storage area. Formalin is delivered to the facility via truck trailer and transferred to onsite storage. Formalin is transferred from onsite storage tankers to a mobile delivery trailer tank which distributes the RS to Specialty Sale\u0092s clients. At the point of delivery of the regulated substance, Specialty Sales is no longer responsible for the regulated substance upon completion of delivery. \nThe limits of emergency response for Specialty Sales employees at the Texas facility is limited to Notification and Spill response. Employees receive regular training for these procedures, and when assignments change, receive training updates. Planned improvements related to procedures for the regulated substance are focused on operation, spill response, and evacuation for employees located at the facility RS storage location."
    }
  ]
